  "observations": [
    "Complete base class has a separate ConchSummoned boolean, SUMMON_TIME and nonserialized local summonedProgress; setSummonedBy sets boolean, summoner UUID and time. But the actual MagicConchItem producer is missing, so no complete call chain or concrete conch cost/owner/target/duration behavior is established.",
    "While summoned, positive time increases progress toward20; server decrements remaining time even during entry. Time reaching0 requests splash61/sound, while later nonpositive-time ticks lower progress and server discard at progress<=0. isEffectiveAi additionally requires progress>=20 when summoned, but does NOT itself test time>0. Since parent super.tick precedes own progress updates, exact AI-entry/withdraw scheduling cannot be inferred without native callers. This is an AI availability gate, not hurt or control immunity.",
    "ConchSummoned is saved unconditionally; UUID and time only when summonerUUID exists. Reads restore UUID/time only if the key is present. Progress, previous progress, trading-lock counter, Mage spin/ranged cooldown, strafe target and animation are not shown in additional NBT. Reconstructed positive lifetime can replay the entry ramp while remaining time continues; original audio/particles/actual AI/time behavior are unverified. Existing-instance absent fields do not imply explicit clearing.",
    "Trading lock setter takes max of incoming/current duration; base tick reduces positive values. Registered attack/disappear goals gate their own canUse on !isTradingLocked, but GoalSelector/continuation/native AI call sites are not expanded. Mage own tick can still run its animation bodies after the parent tick; a false effective-AI result is not evidence every subclass effect/attack callback is suppressed.",
    "Mage renderer translates a summoned body by normalized progress and uses ordinary/sepia/outline material branches. Its glow layer has constant alpha1 behind invisibility check; this source does not show glow switched specifically by AI lock, damage refusal or invulnerability. Actual model transforms, material factory implementation, sound engine, networking and pixels were not expanded/run.",
    "Mage subclass grants causeFallDamage=false and conditional noGravity; base isInvulnerableTo adds only IN_WALL beside parent. Those local constants do not prove summon/entry/withdraw invulnerability. BUBBLED add/remove requests in own tick are unchecked and the actual effect implementation is not expanded; attack WaterBolt/Wave effects and downstream hurt results are context0, not complete additional mechanisms.",
    "Old reputation decision already covers successful-hurt reputation bands, helpful retaliation refusal and owner reaction; this whole old family is not counted again. Separate ordinary body/attack animations, parameters, entity variants and render modes confer no credit. Summoned ownership/finite lifetime is also compared against existing AoA minion owner-bound expiry; missing producer and caller evidence prevents claiming the new unit is distinct and complete.",
    "Complete base also saves SwappedItem but reads SwappedWeapon in the shown methods. This is a local upstream serialization observation, not a reproduced Dynasty defect or permission to copy/fix upstream code. Trade loot/altar item restoration and all external state ownership remain outside this partial summon-gate proposal."
  ],
